	(text "CV DAC"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 17.78 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "24f96668-2732-5604-bf7d-2cb049ff7c19")
	)
	(text "DAC8568 grade A: 0-2.5 V from its internal reference (off at power-up), outputs reset to zero. Each stage: non-inverting\ngain 1 + 33k/10k = 4.3, offset by OFFSET_REF = VREF × 22k/34k through the 10 kΩ: Vout = 4.3·Vdac − 5.34 V, so −5.34 V …\n+5.41 V, putting ±5 V inside the DAC's specified codes (0 V at code ≈ 32544). The offset tracks the DAC's own reference, as\nin Performer, O&C, Marbles and Stages. CVO7/8: the 1 kΩ sits inside the loop (feedback from the jack side, as Mutable\ndoes), so the jack holds its voltage under load. CV1-6 go through the DG412 switch; firmware corrects their load sag\nusing the ADC, which reads the jack. ±10 V variant (not Rev A): Rf 75k, divider 15k/20k, all Basic: gain 8.5,\nOFFSET_REF 1.429 V, −10.71 … +10.54 V; needs ≥ 10 kΩ loads. The TL074H can swing it."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font (size 1.5 1.5))
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "641fbfe2-59fd-5516-9a2e-190f3a68ae3e")
	)
